{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019rrhYeQke5NZiz9dhb76QT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Weight-editing task (step 3 of 3)\n2\t\n3\tYou are editing part of a neural network BY HAND. Do not train it.\n4\t\n5\t## The model\n6\tLaya is a decision model. For a customer message it routes to one of 5 support\n7\tdepartments: cards, disputes, transfers_topups, fees_fx, account_security. A frozen encoder turns (message, option) into one\n8\t1024-number vector per option (the \"marker vector\"). A small scorer gives each\n9\toption a logit; the highest logit wins. You edit ONLY the scorer.\n10\t\n11\t- `scorer_in.npz`: scorer weights. Scorer = LayerNorm(ln_w, ln_b) -> W1 (1024x1024),\n12\t  b1 -> GELU -> W2 (1024x1), b2. You may also add a ReLU module on the raw marker\n13\t  vector: arrays extra_W0, extra_b0, extra_W1, extra_b1, ... (ReLU between layers,\n14\t  last layer has 1 output); its output is added to the logit.\n15\t- `scorer.py`: `load`, `save`, `logits(S, M)`, `predict(S, M)`.\n16\t- `embed.py`: run the frozen encoder on messages you write yourself:\n17\t  `<lab>/.venv/bin/python embed.py out.npz \"message\" ...` -> out.npz with M [n, 5, 1024].\n18\t- `evidence.csv` + `evidence_M.npz`: 32 labelled customer messages for this\n19\t  correction and their marker vectors (same order).\n20\tUse this Python, which has numpy and torch: `<lab>/.venv/bin/python`\n21\t\n22\t## Department descriptions given to the model\n23\t- cards: getting, activating, delivering, replacing or using a payment card; PIN, contactless, virtual and disposable cards, Apple Pay or Google Pay, lost or stolen cards\n24\t- disputes: a payment, withdrawal or debit the customer does not recognise, was declined, is pending, was charged twice or reverted; refunds\n25\t- transfers_topups: sending or receiving money, bank transfers, topping up the account, balance not updated after a transfer or deposit\n26\t- fees_fx: fees and charges, exchange rates, currency exchange, supported currencies\n27\t- account_security: identity verification, passcode, personal details, closing the account, lost phone, age or country eligibility\n28\t\n29\t## Corrections already applied in earlier steps (must stay true)\n30\t1. Complaints that a card payment or a cash withdrawal used a bad or wrong exchange rate belong to fees_fx, not disputes, even when the customer says the amount looks wrong.\n31\t2. Anything about a card PIN, such as changing the PIN or a PIN that is blocked, belongs to cards, not account_security.\n32\t\n33\t## New correction for this step\n34\tQuestions about who may open or use an account, such as age limits or which countries are supported, belong to account_security, not cards.\n35\t\n36\t## What to do\n37\tWrite `scorer_out.npz` (same format) so that the model:\n38\t1. follows the new correction for all such messages, not only the examples;\n39\t2. still follows every earlier correction;\n40\t3. otherwise routes exactly as `scorer_in.npz` does.\n41\tA hidden test set of 3,080 real customer messages scores all three.\n42\t\n43\t## Rules\n44\t- Allowed: read weights, run the scorer and the encoder on inputs you choose,\n45\t  reason about directions and units, change any scorer weights, add the extra module.\n46\t- Not allowed: gradient descent, optimizers, any training or fitting loop,\n47\t  least squares, logistic regression or any solver fitted to data. Every weight\n48\t  you write must come from your own reasoning. Computing a direction as a\n49\t  difference of means of marker vectors of messages YOU wrote is allowed;\n50\t  fitting to the evidence labels is not. Checking with forward passes is fine.\n51\t- Write `NOTES.md`: what you changed and why, in under 200 words.\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec93677f-267e-4bb2-baab-e277676defcb","uuid":"a0131c6b-9a88-46f9-8825-8a9c5664a63a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T20:22:01.064Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"$WSROOT/laya/s1/fable-high-r2/step3/TASK.md","content":"# Weight-editing task (step 3 of 3)\n\nYou are editing part of a neural network BY HAND. Do not train it.\n\n## The model\nLaya is a decision model. For a customer message it routes to one of 5 support\ndepartments: cards, disputes, transfers_topups, fees_fx, account_security. A frozen encoder turns (message, option) into one\n1024-number vector per option (the \"marker vector\"). A small scorer gives each\noption a logit; the highest logit wins. You edit ONLY the scorer.\n\n- `scorer_in.npz`: scorer weights. Scorer = LayerNorm(ln_w, ln_b) -> W1 (1024x1024),\n  b1 -> GELU -> W2 (1024x1), b2. You may also add a ReLU module on the raw marker\n  vector: arrays extra_W0, extra_b0, extra_W1, extra_b1, ... (ReLU between layers,\n  last layer has 1 output); its output is added to the logit.\n- `scorer.py`: `load`, `save`, `logits(S, M)`, `predict(S, M)`.\n- `embed.py`: run the frozen encoder on messages you write yourself:\n  `<lab>/.venv/bin/python embed.py out.npz \"message\" ...` -> out.npz with M [n, 5, 1024].\n- `evidence.csv` + `evidence_M.npz`: 32 labelled customer messages for this\n  correction and their marker vectors (same order).\nUse this Python, which has numpy and torch: `<lab>/.venv/bin/python`\n\n## Department descriptions given to the model\n- cards: getting, activating, delivering, replacing or using a payment card; PIN, contactless, virtual and disposable cards, Apple Pay or Google Pay, lost or stolen cards\n- disputes: a payment, withdrawal or debit the customer does not recognise, was declined, is pending, was charged twice or reverted; refunds\n- transfers_topups: sending or receiving money, bank transfers, topping up the account, balance not updated after a transfer or deposit\n- fees_fx: fees and charges, exchange rates, currency exchange, supported currencies\n- account_security: identity verification, passcode, personal details, closing the account, lost phone, age or country eligibility\n\n## Corrections already applied in earlier steps (must stay true)\n1. Complaints that a card payment or a cash withdrawal used a bad or wrong exchange rate belong to fees_fx, not disputes, even when the customer says the amount looks wrong.\n2. Anything about a card PIN, such as changing the PIN or a PIN that is blocked, belongs to cards, not account_security.\n\n## New correction for this step\nQuestions about who may open or use an account, such as age limits or which countries are supported, belong to account_security, not cards.\n\n## What to do\nWrite `scorer_out.npz` (same format) so that the model:\n1. follows the new correction for all such messages, not only the examples;\n2. still follows every earlier correction;\n3. otherwise routes exactly as `scorer_in.npz` does.\nA hidden test set of 3,080 real customer messages scores all three.\n\n## Rules\n- Allowed: read weights, run the scorer and the encoder on inputs you choose,\n  reason about directions and units, change any scorer weights, add the extra module.\n- Not allowed: gradient descent, optimizers, any training or fitting loop,\n  least squares, logistic regression or any solver fitted to data. Every weight\n  you write must come from your own reasoning. Computing a direction as a\n  difference of means of marker vectors of messages YOU wrote is allowed;\n  fitting to the evidence labels is not. Checking with forward passes is fine.\n- Write `NOTES.md`: what you changed and why, in under 200 words.\n","numLines":52,"startLine":1,"totalLines":52}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019rrhYeQke5NZiz9dhb76QT","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
