{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RhM8TZkjniUCv4wrh2DVj9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Step 2 notes\n2\t\n3\t**Change.** The original scorer and the step-1 pathway of the extra module are untouched. I appended a second, block-diagonal pathway (4 -> 2 -> 1 units) that adds `e2 = 6 * min(gate_slot, gate_topic)` to the logit.\n4\t\n5\t- Units: PCA of my own marker vectors; each component is measured in units of its own standard deviation (\"standardized PCs\"). In raw units the two giant components drown the topic signal.\n6\t- `gate_slot`: projection on the difference of means \"cards slot minus other slots\" (PCs 2-63). Perfectly separable on held-out halves, so the module is silent on the other four slots.\n7\t- `gate_topic`: projection on \"my 148 PIN messages minus my 378 non-PIN messages, cards slot\" (PCs 2-255).\n8\t- Both gates are clipped ramps; `min` is built as `a - relu(a - b)`.\n9\t\n10\t**Checks (build.py).** Evidence: 15/16 PIN messages now route to cards (miss: \"my pin has been compromised\"), 0/16 others changed, the step-1 exchange-rate correction unchanged (64/76 before and after). Split-half on my own messages: 95% of held-out PIN messages flip, about 3 of 189 contrast messages change, all baseline-borderline. Only means, standard deviations, percentiles and forward passes were used.\n11\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec93677f-267e-4bb2-baab-e277676defcb","uuid":"9740ede7-95cd-4092-9bbb-78c573be2f2a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T20:22:29.520Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"$WSROOT/laya/s1/fable-high-r2/step2/NOTES.md","content":"# Step 2 notes\n\n**Change.** The original scorer and the step-1 pathway of the extra module are untouched. I appended a second, block-diagonal pathway (4 -> 2 -> 1 units) that adds `e2 = 6 * min(gate_slot, gate_topic)` to the logit.\n\n- Units: PCA of my own marker vectors; each component is measured in units of its own standard deviation (\"standardized PCs\"). In raw units the two giant components drown the topic signal.\n- `gate_slot`: projection on the difference of means \"cards slot minus other slots\" (PCs 2-63). Perfectly separable on held-out halves, so the module is silent on the other four slots.\n- `gate_topic`: projection on \"my 148 PIN messages minus my 378 non-PIN messages, cards slot\" (PCs 2-255).\n- Both gates are clipped ramps; `min` is built as `a - relu(a - b)`.\n\n**Checks (build.py).** Evidence: 15/16 PIN messages now route to cards (miss: \"my pin has been compromised\"), 0/16 others changed, the step-1 exchange-rate correction unchanged (64/76 before and after). Split-half on my own messages: 95% of held-out PIN messages flip, about 3 of 189 contrast messages change, all baseline-borderline. Only means, standard deviations, percentiles and forward passes were used.\n","numLines":11,"startLine":1,"totalLines":11}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RhM8TZkjniUCv4wrh2DVj9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
